$technology_desc_hull_cruiser_17;Unlocks 15,000t Light Cruisers
$technology_desc_hull_cruiser_18;Unlocks 16,000t Light Cruisers
$technology_desc_hull_cruiser_19;Unlocks 17,000t Light Cruisers
$technology_desc_hull_cruiser_20;Unlocks 18,000t Light Cruisers
$component_name_short_propellant_0_1;Nitrocell
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_17_1; Nitrocell Poudre-B Experimental Charge
$technology_desc_projectile_explosive_17_1;An early experimental application of nitrocellulose derived from texting with Poudre B chemistry. While offering improved ballistic performance over traditional powders, its poor chemical stability and sensitivity make it risky in prolonged storage and limit large-scale adoption.
$component_name_short_propellant_6_1;EGDN Nitroglycol
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_23_1;EGDN Bursting Charge Mixture
$technology_desc_projectile_explosive_23_1;A high-energy explosive mixture based on nitroglycol (EGDN), delivering greater explosive power and improved detonation characteristics. Its volatility and temperature sensitivity require reinforced ammunition handling and storage systems.
$component_name_short_explosive_9_1;Pure RDX
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_16_1;Full RDX Component Propellant
$technology_desc_projectile_explosive_16_1;A pure RDX-based explosive component providing exceptional brisance and shell lethality. Although highly effective, its strength demands advanced safety measures and precise fusing. It promises insanely explosive outcomes.
$component_name_short_explosive_0_1;Compressed Black Powder
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_7_1;Compressed Black Powder Propellant
$technology_desc_projectile_explosive_7_1;Black powder compressed into dense charges to improve consistency and shell efficiency. While damages becomes more reliable than with looser powder mixtures, it remains a low explosive with limited destructive potential compared to more modern compounds. The Pressurization also make it less stable in storage and prone for premature explosion. Handle with care.
$component_name_short_he_5; Explosive Incendiary
$component_name_short_shell_S.light;Sub-Caliber
$technology_name_projectile_shell_11_1;Sub Caliber Sabot Shells
$technology_desc_projectile_shell_11_1;A sub-caliber projectile using a sabot to achieve much higher muzzle velocity and penetration at the cost of Explosiveness. Extremely effective against armor, but reduced post-penetration damage.
$component_name_short_he_1_1;Incendiary
$technology_name_projectile_shell_22_1;Incendiary Shell
$technology_desc_projectile_shell_22_1;An incendiary-filled shell soley designed to ignite fires on impact and spread damage across exposed areas. Most effective against lightly protected targets or superstructures.
$component_name_short_he_0_1;Stabilized CNF
$technology_name_projectile_shell_23_1;High Explosive Nose Fuse Fin Stabilized Round
$technology_desc_projectile_shell_23_1;A fin-stabilized high explosive round that maintains accuracy at long range. Improved flight stability enhances range and consistency.
$component_name_short_ap_3_1;Capped Semi
$technology_name_projectile_shell_26_1;Semi AP Shell Capped
$technology_desc_projectile_shell_26_1;A semi-armor-piercing shell fitted with a cap to slightly improve penetration on angled armor. Balances armor defeat with reliable internal damage after penetration.
$component_name_short_ap_0_1;Improved AP
$technology_name_projectile_shell_28_1;Improved AP Shell
$technology_desc_projectile_shell_28_1;A shape-improved standard un-capped armor-piercing shell with optimized travel, penetration and material quality. Offers higher damage and overall better performance.
$component_name_short_turret_traverse_0_1;Improved
$technology_name_gun_mech_9;Improved Turret Design
$technology_desc_gun_mech_9;Refined turret structures and improved bearing layouts reduce mechanical stress and improves firing stability. The design increases reliability and accuracy, especially in rough sea conditions.
$component_name_short_turret_traverse_1_1;Early Stabilizer
$technology_name_gun_mech_2_1;Early Turret Stabilizer
$technology_desc_gun_mech_2_1;An early mechanical stabilizer that partially compensates for ship roll. It improves gun handling but offers limited effectiveness in heavy seas.
$component_name_short_turret_traverse_1_2;Electrical Stab.
$technology_name_gun_mech_2_2;Electrical Stabilizer
$technology_desc_gun_mech_2_2;An electrically assisted stabilization system that reacts faster to ship movement. Provides more consistent gun alignment during moderate wave action.
$component_name_short_turret_traverse_1_3;2-Axis Stabilizer
$technology_name_gun_mech_2_3;two-axis Stabilizer
$technology_desc_gun_mech_2_3;A two-axis stabilization system that actively compensates for pitch and roll. Significantly improves accuracy while firing in rough seas and during maneuvering.
$component_name_short_turret_traverse_1_4;3-Axis Stabilizer
$technology_name_gun_mech_2_4;three-axis Stabilizer
$technology_desc_gun_mech_2_4;An advanced three-axis stabilizer compensating for pitch, roll, and yaw. Enables accurate fire even in heavy seas.
$component_name_short_barbette_thickness_1;Armored
$component_name_short_barbette_thickness_2;Armored II
$component_name_short_barbette_thickness_3;Armored III
$component_name_short_barbette_thickness_5;Armored IV
$component_name_short_barbette_thickness_5_1;Electrical
$technology_name_gun_layout_23_1;Electrically Powered Barbette
$technology_desc_gun_layout_23_1;Electric motors replace manual systems for rotating and elevating the barbette. This improves response time, reduces crew workload, and ensures more reliable operation under combat conditions.
$component_name_short_barbette_thickness_4;Electrical II
$technology_name_gun_layout_22;Electrically Powered Barbette II
$technology_desc_gun_layout_22;Electric motors replace manual systems for rotating and elevating the barbette. This improves response time, reduces crew workload, and ensures more reliable operation under combat conditions.
$component_name_short_barbette_thickness_5_2;Electrical III
$technology_name_gun_layout_23_2;Electrically Powered Barbette III
$technology_desc_gun_layout_23_2;Electric motors replace manual systems for rotating and elevating the barbette. This improves response time, reduces crew workload, and ensures more reliable operation under combat conditions.
$technology_desc_projectile_explosive_43;A new chemical substance increases the explosiveness of Shell fillers, affecting the Damage of HE shells
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_43;Increased HE Filler I
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_44;Increased HE Filler II
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_45;Increased HE Filler III
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_46;Increased HE Filler IV
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_47;Increased HE Filler V
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_48;Increased HE Filler VI
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_49;Safe Storage Shells
$technology_desc_projectile_explosive_49;With individual sub-packing it is possible to reduce the chance of spreading Damage when Storages are hit
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_50;Safety Containing
$technology_desc_projectile_explosive_50;Increased safety protocols in storing ammunition reduces explosion chances
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_51;Liquid Storage Applications
$technology_desc_projectile_explosive_51;Liquid Storage technology surrounds the Storage with water-like mixture reserves that automatically flood the storage when penetrated. This gives a massively reduced chance of devastating explosions while retaining most of the storage space, but increases the weight considerably.
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_52;Secured extra Storage
$technology_desc_projectile_explosive_52;Increases storage and reduces the explosions chance by making sure ammunitions is split on multiple smaller storages throughout the ship.
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_53;Safely stored Reserve Torpedo
$technology_desc_projectile_explosive_53;Reduces the chance of explosion while carrying one spare torpedo per launcher
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_54;Maximum Torpedo Storage
$technology_desc_projectile_explosive_54;Redistributes space on the ship to fully maximize torpedo carrying capacity, not considering safety at all.
$technology_name_projectile_explosive_55;Sealed Torpedo Storage Containers
$technology_desc_projectile_explosive_55;By mounting sealed Containers it is possible to carry a higher Torpedo load while reducing risk of devastating damage
$component_name_short_multi_bottom_3;Liquid filled System
$technology_name_surv_hull_3_1;Liquid-Filled Anti-Torpedo Hull System
$technology_desc_surv_hull_3_1;Fuel or water layers absorb explosive energy and reduce hull damage. Massively improves torpedo protection due to blast mitigation but increases leaking chance after hit, fire risk due to non-water liquid components and maintenance complexity in routine dock inspections as well as post-battle.
$component_name_short_multi_bottom_4;Cellular Structured
$technology_name_surv_hull_3_2;Cellular Compartmentalized Hull
$technology_desc_surv_hull_3_2;A cellular internal layout localizes flooding and structural damage. Improves post-hit survivability at the cost of weight and build complexity.
$component_name_short_multi_bottom_5;Multi Layered
$technology_name_surv_hull_3_3;Blast-Absorbing Hull
$technology_desc_surv_hull_3_3;A specially manufactured multi-layered outer plating spaced armored hull that was designed to dissipate explosive force on several layers. Highly effective against mines and torpedoes but very costly to repair after damage.
$component_name_short_multi_bottom_6;Double Cellular
$technology_name_surv_hull_3_4;Cellular Compartmentalized Double Hull
$technology_desc_surv_hull_3_4;A double cellular internal layout maximizsed flooding prevention and minimizes structural damage. Greatly improves post-hit survivability at the cost of weight and massive build complexity.
$component_name_short_multi_bottom_0_1;Improved
$technology_name_surv_hull_1_1;Improved Inner Hull
$technology_desc_surv_hull_1_1;Improves torpedo protection but increases construction time and maintenance complexity.
$component_name_short_boiler_4_1;Water Tube
$compTypes_name_short_antiflooding;Damage Control
$compTypes_name_antiflooding;Damage Control
$component_name_short_Anti_Flooding_1_1;Anti Fire
$technology_name_surv_internal_8_1;Dedicated Fire Suppression Stations
$technology_desc_surv_internal_8_1;Dedicated fire suppression stations enable rapid response to onboard fires. Reduces fire spread and damage through improved equipment and crew coordination.
$component_name_short_Anti_Flooding_3_1;Allround
$technology_name_surv_internal_10_1;Fire & Flood Multi Suppression Systems
$technology_desc_surv_internal_10_1;Integrated systems combine fire suppression with active flooding control. Improves overall damage control efficiency during complex combat damage situations.
$component_name_short_buklheads_0_1;Sealed
$technology_name_surv_internal_2_1;Sealed-Tight Bulkheads
$technology_desc_surv_internal_2_1;Improved sealing and structural reinforcement reduce progressive flooding. Enhances survivability with minimal weight and cost increase.
$component_name_short_buklheads_2_1;Armored
$technology_name_surv_internal_4_1;Internal Armored Bulkhead Protection
$technology_desc_surv_internal_4_1;Armored internal bulkheads absorb blast effects and limit damage spread. Increases resistance to torpedo and shell hits at higher weight.
$component_name_short_buklheads_2_2;Armored II
$technology_name_surv_internal_4_2;Advanced Armored Compartmentalization
$technology_desc_surv_internal_4_2;Heavily armored and optimized bulkheads localize severe damage. Greatly improves post-hit survivability but increases construction complexity.
$technology_name_engine_boiler_9_1;Water-tubed Boiler technology
$technology_desc_engine_boiler_9_1;Water-tube boilers improve steam generation speed and reduce weight compared to fire-tube designs. They allow higher power output but require more careful maintenance.
$component_name_short_boiler_4_2;High Pressured
$technology_name_engine_boiler_9_2;Superheated, high pressure Boiler
$technology_desc_engine_boiler_9_2;High-pressure boilers use superheated steam to significantly improve efficiency and engine performance. Increased operating stress demands skilled crews and advanced maintenance.
$component_name_short_boiler_4_3;All-in-One
$technology_name_engine_boiler_9_3;All in one boiler technology
$technology_desc_engine_boiler_9_3;All in one Monotube boilers generate steam in a single pass at extremely high pressure, enabling rapid power response. Their complexity and sensitivity limit them to advanced vessels.
$component_name_short_fuel_coal_2;Processed Coal
$technology_name_engine_boiler_1_1;Processed Coal fuel improvements
$component_name_short_fuel_oil_1_1;Semi-Oil II
$technology_name_engine_boiler_2_1;Improved Semi Coal-Oil
$technology_desc_engine_boiler_1_1;Improved coal processing and firing methods reduce smoke and increase fuel efficiency. These advances allow coal-powered engines to remain competitive.
$technology_desc_engine_boiler_2_1;Refined mixed-fuel systems combine coal and oil to improve combustion control and engine responsiveness. This transitional technology offers better performance without full reliance on oil supplies.
$component_name_short_fuel_oil_1_2;Diesel
$technology_name_engine_boiler_2_2;Diesel Fuel Refinement
$technology_desc_engine_boiler_2_2;Refined diesel fuel improves combustion efficiency and reliability in engines. It enables longer ranges on less consumption, reduced smoke output, and more stable operation compared to earlier fuel oils. Yet, it is not cheap.
$component_name_short_fuel_nuclear_1;Nuclear
$technology_name_engine_boiler_90;Nuclear Power Fuel Source Development
$technology_desc_engine_boiler_90;The development of controlled nuclear fuel enables sustained energy generation without conventional fuel consumption. While offering unmatched endurance and reduced emissions, nuclear fuel demands complex handling, shielding, and long-term maintenance.
$component_name_short_main_engine_90;Nuclear Power Plant
$technology_name_engine_engine_90;Nuclear Power Plant Trials
$technology_desc_engine_engine_90;Experimental nuclear power plants integrate reactors with steam turbines to propel large warships for extended periods. These trials prove exceptional range and reliability, but reveal high construction costs, safety constraints, and limited power responsiveness.
$component_name_short_main_engine_1_1;Steam 2-Exp
$technology_name_engine_engine_1_1;Double Expansion Steam Engines
$technology_desc_engine_engine_1_1;Refined cylinders and better valve gear improve efficiency and reliability. Reduced fuel waste increases range at modest speeds.
$component_name_short_main_engine_6_1;Turbo Electric II
$technology_name_engine_engine_8_1;Advanced Turbo-Electric Propulsion
$technology_desc_engine_engine_8_1;Improved generators and controls increase endurance and power stability. Excellent low-speed handling, but complex and maintenance-heavy.
$technology_desc_engine_engine_7;An engine which uses a steam turbine and special electric motors to convert mechanical energy into power for the drive shafts. Additionally, a portion of the mechanical energy is efficiently converted into electrical power, which supplies vital ship mechanisms.n\The turbo-electric drive offers increased ship maneuverability, survivability, and engine reliability due to the overall efficiency and flexibility of its power distribution. However, turbo-electric drive engines have a much lower horsepower-to-weight ratio.
$component_name_short_main_engine_6_2;Pressured G. Turbines II
$technology_name_engine_engine_8_2;High-Pressure Steam Turbine Plant
$technology_desc_engine_engine_8_2;Superheated high-pressure steam boosts speed and efficiency significantly. Higher stresses increase vibration and maintenance demands.
$component_name_short_main_engine_8_1;Diesel-Electric Drive
$technology_name_engine_engine_10_1;Diesel-Electric Propulsion Systems
$technology_desc_engine_engine_10_1;Diesel generators power electric motors for smooth, efficient thrust control. Lower peak acceleration, but excellent endurance and low smoke.
$component_name_short_main_engine_10;Gas Turbines II
$technology_name_engine_engine_12;Advanced Gas Turbine Technology
$technology_desc_engine_engine_12;Improved compressors and turbine materials increase power and response. High output comes with high vibrations and careful maintenance requirements.
$technology_name_engine_engine_11;Gas Turbine Technology
$compTypes_name_torpedo_prop;Torpedo Propulsion & Variants
$compTypes_name_short_torpedo_prop; Torp Variant
$component_name_short_ammo_shell_normal_safe;Secured Shells
$component_name_short_ammo_shell_less_safe;Dispersed Ammo
$component_name_short_ammo_shell_wetstorage;Liquid Storage
$component_name_short_ammo_shell_more_safe;Increased Safety
$component_name_short_torp_shell_normal_safe;Reserve Storage
$component_name_short_torp_shell_more_super;Maximum
$component_name_short_torp_shell_more_safe;Sealed Storage
$component_name_short_torpedo_prop_elite;Elite
$component_name_short_torpedo_prop_slow;Slowed
$component_name_short_torpedo_prop_longlance;Long Lance
$component_name_short_torpedo_prop_swarm;Autoloader
$component_name_short_torpedo_prop_fastoxygen;Fast Oxygen
$component_name_short_torpedo_prop_hyperlance;Hyper Lance
$component_name_short_torpedo_prop_stealth;Stealth
$technology_name_torpedo_prop_3;Stealth Torpedoes
$technology_desc_torpedo_prop_3;Putting in silent running electric motors gives these Torpedoes the ability to run nearly undetected
$technology_name_torpedo_prop_4;Elite Torpedoes
$technology_desc_torpedo_prop_4;Combining the best developed technologies gives these Torpedoes one of the best traits and makes them very versatile. Reload is slightly increased due to complexity of the system
$technology_name_torpedo_prop_16;Slowed Torpedoes
$technology_desc_torpedo_prop_16;Slowing early torpedoes gives them the ability to travel way further and reduces detectability slightly. Still, its not difficult for a ship to evade them. Use wisely"
$technology_name_torpedo_prop_17;Long Lance Torpedoes
$technology_desc_torpedo_prop_17;Long Lance Technology gives increased range and speed, which makes them more effective in theory, yet it also makes them easier to see and just slightly less destructive.
$technology_name_torpedo_prop_18;Autoloading Torpedo Tubes
$technology_desc_torpedo_prop_18;Autoloaded Throwers are fit with a semi automatic reload system on shortened throwers which gives massively increased reload and range, but several drawbacks like massively reduced Accuracy
$technology_desc_torpedo_prop_19;Fast Oxygen
$technology_name_torpedo_prop_19;Improved Version of the Fast torpedo, with slightly increased range and speed while staying less visible. Very effective when given the opportunity.
$technology_name_torpedo_prop_20;Hyper Lance
$technology_desc_torpedo_prop_20;Super Long Lance Technology gives even more increased range and speed, which and counters some of their drawbacks like visibility and accuracy making them a great choice. They stay just slightly less effective in destructability than regular Torpedoes
$technology_name_torpedo_tubes_17;Cruiser Single Torpedo
$technology_desc_torpedo_tubes_17;Single Deck Torpedoes become available for Cruisers
$technology_name_torpedo_tubes_18;Destroyer Double Torpedoes
$technology_desc_torpedo_tubes_18;Double Deck Torpedoes become available for Destroyers
$technology_name_torpedo_tubes_19;Destroyer Triple Torpedoes
$technology_desc_torpedo_tubes_19;Triple Deck Torpedoes become available for Destroyers
$technology_name_torpedo_tubes_20;Capital Double Torpedoes
$technology_desc_torpedo_tubes_20;Double Deck Torpedoes become available for Capital Ships
$technology_name_torpedo_tubes_21;Destroyer Quadruple Torpedoes
$technology_desc_torpedo_tubes_21;Quadruple Deck Torpedoes become available for Destroyers
$technology_name_torpedo_tubes_22;Cruiser Quadruple Torpedoes
$technology_desc_torpedo_tubes_22;Quadruple Deck Torpedoes become available for Cruisers
$technology_name_torpedo_tubes_23;Destroyer Quintruple Torpedoes
$technology_desc_torpedo_tubes_23;Quintruple Deck Torpedoes become available for Destroyers
$technology_name_torpedo_tubes_24;Torpedo Tube Improvement Tech I
$technology_desc_torpedo_tubes_24;Torpedo Tubes get improved by new Technology, making them better but slightly more expensive
$technology_name_torpedo_tubes_25;Torpedo Tube Improvement Tech II
$technology_name_torpedo_tubes_26;Torpedo Tube Improvement Tech III
$technology_name_torpedo_tubes_27;Torpedo Tube Improvement Tech IV
$technology_name_torpedo_tubes_28;Torpedo Tube Improvement Tech V
$technology_name_torpedo_size_11;Improved 21-Inch Torpedos
$technology_desc_torpedo_size_11;Improved 21 Inch Torpedo technology giving older Launchers a lot more Firepower and versatility
$technology_name_torpedo_size_12;Improved 18-Inch Torpedos
$technology_desc_torpedo_size_12;Improved 18 Inch Torpedo technology giving older Launchers a lot more Firepower and versatility
$technology_name_torpedo_size_13;Improved 24-Inch Torpedos
$technology_desc_torpedo_size_13;Improved 24 Inch Torpedo technology giving older Launchers a lot more Firepower and versatility
$technology_name_torpedo_size_14;Modern 21-Inch Torpedos
$technology_desc_torpedo_size_14;Modernized 21 Inch Torpedo launchers fully refitting old tech with modern standards, further increasing firepower
$technology_name_torpedo_size_15;Modern 18-Inch Torpedos
$technology_desc_torpedo_size_15;Modernized 18 Inch Torpedo launchers fully refitting old tech with modern standards, further increasing firepower
$technology_name_torpedo_size_16;Modern 24.5-Inch Torpedos
$technology_desc_torpedo_size_16;Modern hightech 24.5 Inch Torpedo launchers giving massive firepower upgrade potential
$component_name_short_torpedo_diameter_6_2;Impr. 21 Inch
$component_name_short_torpedo_diameter_3_2;Impr. 18 Inch
$component_name_short_torpedo_diameter_9_2;Impr. 24 Inch
$component_name_short_torpedo_diameter_6_3;Modern 21 Inch
$component_name_short_torpedo_diameter_3_3;Modern 18 Inch
$component_name_short_torpedo_diameter_9_3;Modern 24.5 Inch
$technology_name_armor_forging_12;Hot Rolled Homogeneous Armor
$technology_desc_armor_forging_12;Standardized hot rolling produced uniform armor plate with predictable ballistic performance.
$technology_name_armor_forging_13;Electric Arc Furnace Steelmaking
$technology_desc_armor_forging_13;Electric furnaces enabled cleaner steels with precise alloy composition control.
$technology_name_armor_forging_14;Controlled Heat Treatment Processes
$technology_desc_armor_forging_14;Precisely timed heating and cooling improved hardness toughness balance.
$technology_name_armor_forging_15;Alloy Steel Optimization
$technology_desc_armor_forging_15;Systematic alloying increased strength while limiting brittleness under impact.
$technology_name_armor_forging_16;Improved Quenching and Tempering
$technology_desc_armor_forging_16;Advanced quenching methods reduced cracking and residual internal stresses.
$technology_name_armor_forging_17;Welded Armor Plate Construction
$technology_desc_armor_forging_17;Welding replaced riveting enabling stronger lighter armored structures.
$technology_name_armor_forging_18;Vacuum Degassed Steel
$technology_desc_armor_forging_18;Vacuum treatment removed gases improving toughness fatigue resistance and consistency.
$technology_name_armor_forging_19;Precision Rolling and Thickness Control
$technology_desc_armor_forging_19;Modern rolling mills achieved tighter tolerances and uniform plate thickness.
$technology_name_armor_forging_20;High Toughness Structural Steels
$technology_desc_armor_forging_20;Postwar steels emphasized toughness ductility and crack resistance under shock.
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_9;Stereoscopic Rangefinder I
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_10;Stereoscopic Rangefinder II
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_11;Stereoscopic Rangefinder III
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_12;Stereoscopic Rangefinder IV
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_13;Stereoscopic Rangefinder V
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_14;Stereoscopic Rangefinder VI
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_6;Coincidence Rangefinder VI
$component_name_short_rangefinder_coinc_6;Coinc-VI
$component_name_short_rangefinder_stereo_6;StereoSc-VI
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_7;Modern Fire Control I
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_8;Modern Fire Control II
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_15;Modern Fire Control III
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_16;Modern Fire Control IV
$component_name_short_rangefinder_coinc_7;Modern FCS I
$component_name_short_rangefinder_coinc_8;Modern FCS II
$component_name_short_rangefinder_stereo_7;Modern FCS III
$component_name_short_rangefinder_stereo_8;Modern FCS IV
$technology_desc_aim_rangefinder_10;Centralized fire control integrates rangefinders into turrets to continuously track targets. Gun laying is coordinated across turrets, improving accuracy.
$technology_desc_aim_rangefinder_11;Mechanical computer-assisted fire control supplements optical tracking with more electronic ranging. Targets can be detected and engaged reliably in poor visibility and at extended ranges.
$technology_desc_aim_rangefinder_12;Improved processing and stabilized directors provide faster target acquisition and more accurate range solutions. Fire control remains effective during heavy maneuvering and adverse sea conditions.
$technology_desc_aim_rangefinder_13;Advanced radar fire control combines precision ranging, stabilized tracking, and refined automated ballistic computation. Engagements are accurate at long range, day or night, with minimal dependence on visual contact.
$technology_desc_aim_rangefinder_9;A stereoscopic Rangefinder of greater lenght and width, offering improved accuracy. It is heavier and more expensive.
$component_name_short_rangefinder_radar_4; Gen IV
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_17;Radar Rangefinder I
$technology_desc_aim_rangefinder_17;The Radar is a revolutionary device using Radiowaves to detect targets over high distances. This technology gives a massive advantage for purpose build ships featuring this device.
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_18;Radar Rangefinder II
$technology_desc_aim_rangefinder_18;A Improved Radar offers increased accuracy over longer Distances
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_19;Radar Rangefinder III
$technology_desc_aim_rangefinder_19;Enhanced Radar technology offers highly increased accuracy over longer Distances
$technology_name_aim_rangefinder_20;Radar Rangefinder IV
$technology_desc_aim_rangefinder_20;Modern Radar technology offers massively increased accuracy over extreme Distances
$component_name_short_armor_0;Iron plate early
$technology_name_armor_quality_1;Early Iron Plate Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_1;First Armor used by Ironclads since the first projects. Not very special, but plentiful and cheap.
$component_name_short_armor_1;Iron Plate
$technology_name_armor_quality_2;Standard Iron Plate Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_2;Improved Armor used by later Ironclads, giving them good survivability while balancing weight and cost.
$component_name_short_armor_2;Iron Plate riveted
$technology_name_armor_quality_3;Advanced Riveted Iron Plate Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_3;Experimental Riveted Iron Armor used early by special projects. It gives better results but is expensive and is somewhat difficult to handle. Very good early protection, but at a price.
$component_name_short_armor_3;Compound
$technology_name_armor_quality_4;Compound Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_4;Compound armor is produced by using multiple layers of different armor to improve protection. Early versions usually tried to mix different iron and steel versions to effectively combine cost and protection.
$component_name_short_armor_4;Nickel-Steel early
$technology_name_armor_quality_5;Early Nickel-Steel Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_5;Nickel-Steel seemed to be the frontrunner for great Armor at this moment and has been developed to give better protection.
$component_name_short_armor_5;Nickel-Steel
$technology_name_armor_quality_6;Nickel-Steel Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_6;Production Variant Nickel-Steel gives great protection slightly reducing cost and effectiveness, giving a great allround armor variant.
$component_name_short_armor_6;Harvey Armor
$technology_name_armor_quality_7;Harvey Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_7;The Harvey Process improves on the Nickel-Steel Armor by hardening the surface. This increases cost but gives way better results in return.
$component_name_short_armor_7;Harvey Compound
$technology_name_armor_quality_8;Harvey Compound Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_8;The Harvey Process improves on the Nickel-Steel Armor by hardening the surface. Adding further Compounding layers gives a great boost on overall effectiveness, but adds complexity to the process. At Massive cost and Production risk, it is a choice but need to be well thought out.
$component_name_short_armor_8;Harvey Experimental
$technology_name_armor_quality_9;Experimental Harvey Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_9;By adding super-hardening into the Harvey Process, the Armor is improved further. Armor effectiveness is above normal Harvey, and the weight is reduced. It further adds complexity to the process making it prone to defects and errors. Massive cost and Production risk but great protection.
$component_name_short_armor_9;Early Krupp
$technology_name_armor_quality_10;Early version Krupp Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_10;First Version of the well-known Krupp armor, adding Chromium and Carbon to the process makes this outstanding armor for its time.
$component_name_short_armor_10;Krupp
$technology_name_armor_quality_11;Standard Krupp Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_11;The Standard Krupp Armor from the early 20th Century. Expensive but very effective.
$component_name_short_armor_11;Krupp I advanced
$technology_name_armor_quality_12;Advanced Krupp I Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_12;Advanced Version of the First Krupp armor Variant, adding special coating and Harvey hardening methods.
$component_name_short_armor_12;Krupp II
$technology_name_armor_quality_13;Krupp II Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_13;Improved Version of the Standard Krupp Armor with new Formula. Still Expensive and still very effective.
$component_name_short_armor_13;Krupp II advanced
$technology_name_armor_quality_14;Advanced Krupp II Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_14;Advancements in the new Krupp II armor Variant are made by adding new trace metals into the Production combined with Harvey-like hardening methods. Very experimental still, and expensive.
$component_name_short_armor_14;Krupp III
$technology_name_armor_quality_15;Krupp III Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_15;Newest Version of the Krupp Armor based on advances in metallurgy making it possible to refine the density and spread of carbon traces. This Variant is so strong, that it was classified as Krupp III, starting a new Era of high powered armor.
$component_name_short_armor_15;Krupp III advanced
$technology_name_armor_quality_16;Advanced Krupp III Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_16;Advancements in Krupp Armor are made by new Production methods and coatings. Improved effectiveness for all applications.
$component_name_short_armor_16;Krupp III super
$technology_name_armor_quality_17;Improved Krupp III Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_17;Super Version of Krupp III Armor. Combining the hardening processes of Harvey Super Armor with newest Advancements in Armor development.
$component_name_short_armor_17;Krupp experimental
$technology_name_armor_quality_18;Experimental late Krupp Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_18;Experimental first version of a Krupp IV Armor which can be considered still in trials. Offers Reduced Armor weight, massive Armor protection and Immense advancements in Structural integrity for ships. Massively expensive and risky to use.
$component_name_short_armor_18;Modern Armor
$technology_name_armor_quality_19;Modern Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_19;Most versatile and modern Ship Armor in the 20th Century. Mass production make this an excellent versatile choice, very effective.
$component_name_short_armor_19;Modern improved
$technology_name_armor_quality_20;Improved Modern Armor 
$technology_desc_armor_quality_20;Advancements in the most Modern armor Variant are made by adding new trace metals into the Production combined with special coat-hardening methods. Very experimental and immensely expensive, yet also lightweight.
$component_name_short_armor_20;Modern experimental
$technology_name_armor_quality_21;Experimental Modern Armor
$technology_desc_armor_quality_21;Experimental Modern Ship Armor. Offers massively Reduced Armor weight, highest Armor protection. Needs special facilities for production and application, making it immensely expensive.
$technology_name_gun_mech_4_1;Turret Control I
$technology_desc_gun_mech_4_1;By making sure that firing and engagement controls are properly set up, it is possible to reduce the rotation time
$technology_name_gun_mech_4_2;Turret Control II
$technology_desc_gun_mech_4_2;By making sure that firing and engagement controls are renewed and readjusted, it is possible to further reduce the rotation time
$techType_name_gun_tech;Gun Components
$techType_tooltip_gun_tech;- Develops loading speed Components for Turrets\n -Develops advancements in turret rotation speeds
$technology_name_hull_construction_15;Massproduction
$technology_desc_hull_construction_15;Mass Production technologies offer increased production speed but adds risk of smaller errors.
$technology_name_hull_construction_16;Automated Production
$technology_desc_hull_construction_16;Automation in production increases production speed further, but may lead to quality shifts and minor issues
$technology_name_hull_construction_17;Factory Docks
$technology_desc_hull_construction_17;Factory style docks offer better output and increases the keels structure due to better production methods but may lead to an increase of defects due massive needs of workforce but shortages in skilled labour
$technology_name_gun_mech_41_1;Main Gun Length Limit on Maximum
$technology_name_gun_mech_18_1;Improved Reload for Twin Turrets I
$technology_name_gun_mech_18_2;Improved Reload for Twin Turrets II
$technology_name_gun_mech_18_3;Improved Reload for Twin Turrets III
$technology_name_gun_mech_21_1;Improved Reload for Triple Turrets I
$technology_name_gun_mech_21_2;Improved Reload for Triple Turrets II
$technology_name_gun_mech_24_1;Improved Reload for All Turrets I
$technology_name_gun_mech_24_2;Improved Reload for All Turrets II
$component_name_short_radio_1_1;Flashing Lamps
$technology_name_tactics_comm_3_1;Light Signaling Communication Room
$technology_desc_tactics_comm_3_1;A dedicated compartment centralizes visual signaling equipment and trained personnel. Improves coordination by reducing delays in transmitting orders across the ship and fleet.
$component_name_short_radio_1;Morse
$technology_name_tactics_comm_3;Wireless Telegraphy
$technology_desc_tactics_comm_3;Early wireless telegraphy enables communication beyond visual range using coded signals. Transmission is slow and vulnerable to interference but greatly extends fleet coordination.
$component_name_short_radio_1_2;Wave Radio
$technology_name_tactics_comm_3_2;Wave Transmission Radio
$technology_desc_tactics_comm_3_2;Continuous wave transmitters provide clearer and more stable signals than spark systems. Messages can be sent faster and over longer distances with improved reliability.
$component_name_short_radio_2_1;Voice Radio
$technology_name_tactics_comm_4_1;Amplitude Modulation Radio
$technology_desc_tactics_comm_4_1;Amplitude modulation enables direct voice communication over radio. Commands can be issued instantly, greatly improving reaction time and tactical flexibility.
$compTypes_name_radio;Signaling
$component_name_short_gun_reload_1;Improved
$technology_name_gun_mech_11;Improved Turret Reload Enhancement
$technology_desc_gun_mech_11;Improving the turret reload by changing turret and gun design to adjust to faster reloading times
$component_name_short_gun_reload_1_1;Loading deck
$technology_name_gun_mech_11_1;Loading Deck Turret Enhancement
$technology_desc_gun_mech_11_1;Adding a loading deck to each turret improve the turrets to be faster in reloading times at the cost of a potential explosive outcome
$component_name_short_gun_reload_2;Early Speedloader
$technology_name_gun_mech_14;Early Turret Speedloading Enhancement
$technology_desc_gun_mech_14;Using the loading deck, adding a speedloader crane and smaller loadingboxes to each turret to further improve the turrets to be faster in reloading times at the cost of a potential explosive outcome
$component_name_short_gun_reload_2_1;Electric Loader
$technology_name_gun_mech_14_1;Electric Turret Loader Enhancement
$technology_desc_gun_mech_14_1;Improving the turret reload by wiring the turret with automated ammunition belts, changing gun designs to maximize reload whilst keeping safety a relevant factor
$component_name_short_gun_reload_3;Speedloader
$technology_name_gun_mech_15;Advanced Turret Speedloading Enhancement
$technology_desc_gun_mech_15;Enhancing the loading deck, adding speedloader cranes and ready racks to each turret to further improve the turrets to be faster in reloading times at the cost of safety
$component_name_short_gun_reload_3_1;Piece by Piece
$technology_name_gun_mech_15_1;Safety-Protocol driven Reloading Measures
$technology_desc_gun_mech_15_1;Increasing turret safety by diespersing Ammunition into pieces which are stored separately until needed and only combined at the barrel one Round at a time. Reload is slowed but it further enhances safety and decreases risk of detonation when the turret is hit
$component_name_short_gun_reload_4;Early Autoloader
$technology_name_gun_mech_16;Early Autoloader Turret Enhancement
$technology_desc_gun_mech_16;Readjusting and combining Loading deck and electrical enhancement to step to a new level by combining both into autoloading feeds for turret reload
$component_name_short_gun_reload_4_1;Autoloader
$technology_name_gun_mech_16_1;Autoloader Turret Enhancement
$technology_desc_gun_mech_16_1;Enhancing early Autoloader technology, boosting autoloading feeds for increased reloading times at the cost of highly reduced turret rotation
$component_name_short_gun_reload_4_2;Impr. Autoloader
$technology_name_gun_mech_16_2;Modern Electric Loader Turret Enhancement
$technology_desc_gun_mech_16_2;Improving the Electically assisted loading technology, further boosting loading times whilst reducing risk and hazards.
$component_name_short_gun_reload_4_3;Modern Autoloader
$technology_name_gun_mech_16_3;Modern Autoloader Turret Enhancement
$technology_desc_gun_mech_16_3;Modern Autoloading tech combining all the advancement steps, perfecting the increase of loading time maximisation, further boosting loading feeds at the cost of massively reduced turret rotation
$Ui_NewGame_DesignUsage_Mixed;AI Design Usage: Hybrid
$Ui_NewGame_DesignUsage_FullGenerated;AI Design Usage: Bespoke
$Ui_NewGame_DesignUsage_FullPredefined;AI Design Usage: Pregenerated
$tooltip_design_usage;<align=center><b><size=125%>AI Ship Generation</b></size></align>\n<b><size=110%>Hybrid</b></size>\nThe initial ships for the campaign are pregenerated but during the campaign the AI designs all of its new ships from scratch.\n\n<b><size=110%>Pregenerated</b></size>\nAll AI designs are pregenerated.\n\n<b><size=110%>Bespoke</b></size>\nAll the AI ships are generated from scratch.
$TAF_LoadError_HarmonyFail_Title;Version Mismatch
$TAF_LoadError_HarmonyFail_Text;The installed version of <b>Tweaks and Fixes</b> doesn't match the installed version of Ultimate Admiral: Dreadnoughts. Patching has failed and your game will not funciton. Please either downgrade UAD to the correct version for your version of TAF, or download the correct version of TAF if available.
$TAF_LoadError_DataFail_Title;TAF Installation Error
$TAF_LoadError_DataFail_Text;<b>Tweaks and Fixes</b> was not installed properly and your game will not function. Please make sure you unzip the correct release of TAF to your Ultimate Admiral: Dreadnoughts folder and overwrite files if prompted. It is not enough to just copy the DLL.
$TAF_Ui_Constr_UpgradeMark;Upgrade Mark
$TAF_Ui_Constr_UpgradeTorpMark;Upgrade\nTorpedo\nMark
